   "id": "tangent-centers",
   "topic": "Minimum parallel track centres on tangent track, by era (prototype feet)",
   "status": "verified",
   "source": "rp71",
   "section": "Modeling eras and recommended minimum tangent track centers",
   "quote": "Old-Time/Narrow Gauge Before 1920 12 feet; Classic 1920 to 1969 13 feet; Early Modern 1969 to 1983 14 feet; Modern After 1983 14 feet",
   "note": "Also stated in RP-7.2. Scaled to N by dividing by 160 (arithmetic, not an NMRA table value): 12 ft = 22.86 mm, 13 ft = 24.77 mm, 14 ft = 26.67 mm. The tables of larger centres for curves (RP-7.2) are pictures and were not read: use these on straight track only.",
   "values": [
