     "name": "old-time_ft",
     "value": 12
    },
    {
     "name": "classic_ft",
     "value": 13
    },
    {
     "name": "modern_ft",
     "value": 14
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "crossover-basis",
   "topic": "Track centres the N turnout crossover data assume",
   "status": "verified",
   "source": "rp1235",
   "section": "Data for crossovers: point of frog to point of frog on parallel tracks",
   "quote": "For Track Centers of: 0.975 (13 prototype feet) ... For Track Center Increment of: 0.075 (1 prototype foot)",
   "note": "0.975 in = 24.765 mm, the plug-in's default spacing, so its crossovers match these tables. 0.075 in = 1.905 mm per prototype foot, which is 304.8 / 160."
  },
  {
   "id": "frog-angle",
   "topic": "Frog number to frog angle",
   "status": "verified",
   "source": "rp1235",
   "section": "(18) Frog Angle (deg.)",
   "quote": "FROG NUMBERS 4 5 6 7 8 ... / Frog Angle (deg.) 14.250 11.421 9.527 8.171 7.153 ...",
   "note": "The table lists 4 to 20. The rule angle = 2 atan(1 / (2 N)) reproduces every listed value to 0.001 degree (checked in core/tests/standards.rs)."
  },
