   "id": "turnout-n-straight",
   "topic": "N scale straight switch turnout: lead, closure radius, switch rail, gage-line offsets",
   "status": "verified",
   "source": "rp1235",
   "section": "RP-12.35 pages 1 and 2, lines (2), (4), (5), (8) to (18), (24) to (26)",
   "quote": "(8) Lead 2.806 3.175 3.544 4.634 5.075 ... ; (11) Curved Rail Radius 7.333 12.245 18.704 23.823 31.944 ... (frog numbers 4 5 6 7 8 ...)",
   "note": "Whole table in `tables.rp12_35` (inches). The plug-in draws the diverging route as the switch rail (straight, at the heel angle), then a closure arc of the listed radius turning to the frog angle, then straight; core/tests/turnouts.rs checks that this reproduces the listed lead and the three gage-line points to 0.1 mm. RP-12.36 (curved switch) is a different design and is not used."
  }
